{"tool_name":"oxypred","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"oxypred","home":"http://webs.iiitd.edu.in/raghava/oxypred/","summary":"Predict the Oxygen Binding Proteins, Which is carrying Erythrocruorin, Hemoglobin, Myoglobin, Hemerithrin, Leghemoglobin and Hemocyanin.","addition_date":"2017-08-03T18:53:24Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T15:36:19.880687Z","tool_type":["Web application"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:oxypred","credit":[{"email":"raghava@imtech.res.in","name":"Dr Gajendra P.S. Raghava","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"],"url":"http://www.imtech.res.in/raghava/oxypred/team.html"}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"http://crdd.osdd.net/raghava/oxypred/help.html"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Sequence classification","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2995"}]}],"name":"Oxypred","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"raghavagps","publication":[{"doi":"10.1016/s1672-0229(08)60012-1","metadata":{"abstract":"This study describes a method for predicting and classifying oxygen-binding proteins. Firstly, support vector machine (SVM) modules were developed using amino acid composition and dipeptide composition for predicting oxygen-binding proteins, and achieved maximum accuracy of 85.5% and 87.8%, respectively. Secondly, an SVM module was developed based on amino acid composition, classifying the predicted oxygen-binding proteins into six classes with accuracy of 95.8%, 97.5%, 97.5%, 96.9%, 99.4%, and 96.0% for erythrocruorin, hemerythrin, hemocyanin, hemoglobin, leghemoglobin, and myoglobin proteins, respectively. Finally, an SVM module was developed using dipeptide composition for classifying the oxygen-binding proteins, and achieved maximum accuracy of 96.1%, 98.7%, 98.7%, 85.6%, 99.6%, and 93.3% for the above six classes, respectively. All modules were trained and tested by five-fold cross validation. Based on the above approach, a web server Oxypred was developed for predicting and classifying oxygen-binding proteins (available from http://www.imtech.res.in/raghava/oxypred/). \u00a9 2008 Beijing Genomics Institute.","authors":[{"name":"Garg A."},{"name":"Muthukrishnan S."},{"name":"Raghava G.P.S."}],"citationCount":8,"date":"2007-03-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Genomics, Proteomics and Bioinformatics","title":"Oxypred: Prediction and Classification of Oxygen-Binding Proteins"},"pmcid":"PMC5054225","pmid":"18267306"}],"topic":[{"term":"Protein structure analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_2814"},{"term":"Proteins","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0078"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"Oxypred","home":"https://bio.tools/oxypred","summary":"Predict the Oxygen Binding Proteins, Which is carrying Erythrocruorin, Hemoglobin, Myoglobin, Hemerithrin, Leghemoglobin and Hemocyanin.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:oxypred/web/webs.iiitd.edu.in","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"sourcecode":{"interpreted":true}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentation":{"manual":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":3,"citations":[{"count":1,"year":"2014"},{"count":1,"year":"2016"},{"count":1,"year":"2018"}],"doi":"10.1016/S1672-0229(08)60012-1","pmcid":"PMC5054225","pmid":"18267306","ref_count":13,"refs":[{"count":1,"year":"2000"},{"count":1,"year":"2003"},{"count":1,"year":"2007"},{"count":2,"year":"2005"},{"count":3,"year":"2004"},{"count":5,"year":"2006"}],"title":"Oxypred: prediction and classification of oxygen-binding proteins.","year":2007}]}],"summary":{"description":true},"website":{"bioschemas":false,"copyright":false,"https":true,"license":false,"operational":200,"redirects":[{"status":301,"url":"https://webs.iiitd.edu.in/raghava/oxypred/"}],"ssl":true,"ssl_err":null}}},{"@id":"https: